§ `Part VII -- Income-related benefits (ss 123-137)`

§§ `s 123 -- income-related benefits`

-- src:2639 | (1) Prescribed schemes shall provide for the following benefits (in this Act referred to as “income-related benefits”)—
-- src:2640 | (a) income support;
-- src:2641 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:2642 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:2643 | (d) housing benefit; and
-- src:2644 | (e) council tax benefit.
@ref s 123(1) (src:2639-2644)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123(1) the benefit is an income-related benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `income support` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `housing benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `council tax benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraphs name three benefits and the text does not say "only"; paragraphs (b) and (c) are blank in this text

-- The duties of s 123(2) to (4) fall on officials; for the person they are rights to be told of, and to see,
-- the scheme.  Each is written twice: as a regulative rule (run with #TRACE, which the stable binary
-- cannot assert) and as a decision function over the facts (which can be asserted).
DECLARE `s 123 Party` IS ONE OF
    `s 123 the Secretary of State`
    `s 123 an authority granting housing benefit`
    `s 123 a billing authority or, in Scotland, a local authority`

DECLARE `s 123 Duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 123 make copies of the scheme available for public inspection without payment`
    `s 123 take the steps that appear appropriate to secure that persons who may be entitled become aware that they may be entitled`

-- src:2645 | (2) The Secretary of State shall make copies of schemes prescribed under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) above available for public inspection at local offices of the Department for Work and Pensions at all reasonable hours without payment.
@ref s 123(2) (src:2645)
`s 123(2) the Secretary of State's duty to make copies of the schemes available` MEANS
    PARTY `s 123 the Secretary of State`
    MUST `s 123 make copies of the scheme available for public inspection without payment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 123 the Secretary of State` BECAUSE "copies of the schemes prescribed under section 123(1)(a), (b) or (c) were not made available for public inspection at local offices of the Department for Work and Pensions at all reasonable hours without payment"

-- src:2645 | (2) The Secretary of State shall make copies of schemes prescribed under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) above available for public inspection at local offices of the Department for Work and Pensions at all reasonable hours without payment.
@ref s 123(2) (src:2645)
GIVEN `the scheme is one prescribed under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is a local office of the Department for Work and Pensions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hour is a reasonable hour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123(2) the person may inspect a copy of the scheme without payment` MEANS
    IF `the scheme is one prescribed under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c)` AND `the place is a local office of the Department for Work and Pensions` AND `the hour is a reasonable hour`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at local offices of the Department for Work and Pensions at all reasonable hours"

-- src:2646 | (3) Every authority granting housing benefit—
-- src:2647 | (a) shall take such steps as appear to them appropriate for the purpose of securing that persons who may be entitled to housing benefit from the authority become aware that they may be entitled to it; and
@ref s 123(3)(a) (src:2646-2647)
`s 123(3)(a) the housing benefit authority's duty to make persons aware` MEANS
    PARTY `s 123 an authority granting housing benefit`
    MUST `s 123 take the steps that appear appropriate to secure that persons who may be entitled become aware that they may be entitled`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 123 an authority granting housing benefit` BECAUSE "the authority did not take the steps that appeared to it appropriate to secure that persons who may be entitled to housing benefit became aware that they may be entitled"

-- src:2646 | (3) Every authority granting housing benefit—
-- src:2647 | (a) shall take such steps as appear to them appropriate for the purpose of securing that persons who may be entitled to housing benefit from the authority become aware that they may be entitled to it; and
@ref s 123(3)(a) (src:2646-2647)
GIVEN `the authority grants housing benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person may be entitled to housing benefit from the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123(3)(a) the authority must take steps so that the person becomes aware` MEANS
    IF `the authority grants housing benefit` AND `the person may be entitled to housing benefit from the authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every authority granting housing benefit ... persons who may be entitled to housing benefit from the authority"

