§§ `s 124 -- income support`

-- The facts s 124(1) reads about the claimant.  The age in paragraph (a) is s 173(a)'s answer, taken separately.
DECLARE `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant` HAS
    `the person is in Great Britain`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has attained the qualifying age for state pension credit`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has no income`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's income in pounds a week`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the applicable amount in pounds a week`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `the person is engaged in remunerative work`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a member of a couple`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other member of the couple is engaged in remunerative work`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is within the 15 days after returning to work with the same employer (section 127(b))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is receiving relevant education`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the circumstances are ones prescribed in which the person may receive relevant education`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person falls within a prescribed category of person`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is entitled to a jobseeker's allowance`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other member of the couple is entitled to a jobseeker's allowance`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the couple are entitled to an income-based jobseeker's allowance`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other member of the couple is entitled to state pension credit`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is entitled to an employment and support allowance`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other member of the couple is entitled to an income-related employment and support allowance` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Paragraph (c), with section 127(b)'s substitution: for 15 days after a return to work with the same
-- employer, paragraph (c) reads only "in the case of a member of a couple, the other member is not engaged in
-- remunerative work".  The substituted paragraph says nothing of a person who is not a member of a couple.
-- Reading taken: the claimant's own work does not bar during the 15 days, and a person who is not in a couple
-- satisfies the substituted paragraph (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2658 | (c) he is not engaged in remunerative work and, if he is a member of a couple, the other member is not so engaged; ...
@ref s 124(1)(c) (src:2658)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 124(1)(c) the person satisfies paragraph (c)` MEANS
    IF facts's `the person is within the 15 days after returning to work with the same employer (section 127(b))`
    THEN (NOT facts's `the person is a member of a couple`) OR (NOT facts's `the other member of the couple is engaged in remunerative work`)
    ELSE    (NOT facts's `the person is engaged in remunerative work`)
        AND ((NOT facts's `the person is a member of a couple`) OR (NOT facts's `the other member of the couple is engaged in remunerative work`))

-- A gloss: income support is for a person in Great Britain who is 16 or over, below the qualifying age for
-- state pension credit, whose income does not exceed the applicable amount, who is not in remunerative work
-- (nor is a partner), is not in relevant education, is in a prescribed category, has no jobseeker's allowance,
-- partner's state pension credit or employment and support allowance.
-- src:2654 | (1) A person in Great Britain is entitled to income support if—
-- src:2655 | (a) he is of or over the age of 16;
-- src:2656 | (aa) he has not attained the qualifying age for state pension credit;
-- src:2657 | (b) he has no income or his income does not exceed the applicable amount;
-- src:2658 | (c) he is not engaged in remunerative work and, if he is a member of a couple, the other member is not so engaged; ...
-- src:2659 | (d) except in such circumstances as may be prescribed, he is not receiving relevant education;
-- src:2660 | (e) he falls within a prescribed category of person; ...
-- src:2661 | (f) he is not entitled to a jobseeker’s allowance and, if he is a member of a couple, the other member of the couple is not, and the couple are not, entitled to an income-based jobseeker’s allowance; ...
-- src:2662 | (g) if he is a member of a couple, the other member of the couple is not entitled to state pension credit; and
-- src:2663 | (h) he is not entitled to an employment and support allowance and, if he is a member of a couple, the other member of the couple is not entitled to an income-related employment and support allowance.
@ref s 124(1) (src:2654-2663)
GIVEN `s 173(a) the person is over 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      facts IS A `s 124(1) Facts about the claimant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person in Great Britain is entitled to income support if" -- a failed condition gives JUST FALSE
    `s 124(1) all of these hold` (LIST
        `the person is in Great Britain`
        , `s 173(a) the person is over 16`
        , `paragraph (aa)`
        , `paragraph (b)`
        , `paragraph (c)`
        , `paragraph (d)`
        , `paragraph (e)`
        , `paragraph (f)`
        , `paragraph (g)`
        , `paragraph (h)`)
    WHERE
        `the person is in Great Britain` MEANS JUST (facts's `the person is in Great Britain`)
        `paragraph (aa)` MEANS JUST (NOT facts's `the person has attained the qualifying age for state pension credit`)
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            JUST (facts's `the person has no income` OR facts's `the person's income in pounds a week` AT MOST facts's `the applicable amount in pounds a week`)
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS JUST (`s 124(1)(c) the person satisfies paragraph (c)` facts)
        `paragraph (d)` MEANS
            JUST ((NOT facts's `the person is receiving relevant education`) OR facts's `the circumstances are ones prescribed in which the person may receive relevant education`)
        `paragraph (e)` MEANS JUST (facts's `the person falls within a prescribed category of person`)
        `paragraph (f)` MEANS
            JUST (    (NOT facts's `the person is entitled to a jobseeker's allowance`)
                  AND (NOT (facts's `the person is a member of a couple` AND facts's `the other member of the couple is entitled to a jobseeker's allowance`))
                  AND (NOT (facts's `the person is a member of a couple` AND facts's `the couple are entitled to an income-based jobseeker's allowance`)))
        `paragraph (g)` MEANS
            JUST (NOT (facts's `the person is a member of a couple` AND facts's `the other member of the couple is entitled to state pension credit`))
        `paragraph (h)` MEANS
            JUST (    (NOT facts's `the person is entitled to an employment and support allowance`)
                  AND (NOT (facts's `the person is a member of a couple` AND facts's `the other member of the couple is entitled to an income-related employment and support allowance`)))

-- (1A): regulations under paragraph (e) must secure that a person who is not a member of a couple and is
-- responsible for, and a member of the same household as, a child under 5 falls within a prescribed category,
-- unless (1B) disapplies (1A).  For the person: she or he is within the category (1)(e) asks about.
-- K2's input is named as the plan names it; the person it asks about is the child.
-- src:2664 | (1A) Regulations under paragraph (e) of subsection (1) must secure that a person who—
-- src:2665 | (a) is not a member of a couple, and
-- src:2666 | (b) is responsible for, and a member of the same household as, a child under the age of 5,
-- src:2667 | falls within a category of person prescribed under that paragraph.
-- src:2668 | (1B) Subsection (1A) does not apply if regulations under subsection (4)(c) of section 1A of the Jobseekers Act 1995 containing the provision mentioned in subsection (5) of that section are in force.
@ref s 124(1A) (src:2664-2668)
GIVEN `the person is not a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is responsible for, and a member of the same household as, a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the person is under 5` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations under section 1A(4)(c) of the Jobseekers Act 1995 containing the provision mentioned in subsection (5) of that section are in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 124(1A) the person falls within a category prescribed under subsection (1)(e)` MEANS
    IF `regulations under section 1A(4)(c) of the Jobseekers Act 1995 containing the provision mentioned in subsection (5) of that section are in force`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1A) does not apply if regulations ... are in force"
    ELSE
        IF `the person is not a member of a couple` AND `the person is responsible for, and a member of the same household as, a child`
        THEN `s 124(1) holds or else nothing` `s 173(a) the person is under 5`
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who— (a) is not a member of a couple, and (b) is responsible for, and a member of the same household as, a child under the age of 5"

-- (4): the amount is the applicable amount, less the person's income if there is any.  A period of less than a
-- week is for the prescribed manner of subsection (5).
-- src:2671 | (4) Subject to subsection (5) below, where a person is entitled to income support, then—
-- src:2672 | (a) if he has no income, the amount shall be the applicable amount; and
-- src:2673 | (b) if he has income, the amount shall be the difference between his income and the applicable amount.
@ref s 124(4) (src:2671-2673)
GIVEN `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has no income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's income in pounds a week` IS A NUMBER
      `the applicable amount in pounds a week` IS A NUMBER
      `the period is less than a week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 124(4) the amount of income support in pounds a week` MEANS
    IF `s 124(1) is known to hold` `s 124(1) the person is entitled to income support`
    THEN
        IF `the period is less than a week`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (5): "calculated in such manner as may be prescribed"
        ELSE
            IF `the person has no income`
            THEN JUST `the applicable amount in pounds a week`
            ELSE
                IF `the person's income in pounds a week` AT MOST `the applicable amount in pounds a week`
                THEN JUST (`the applicable amount in pounds a week` MINUS `the person's income in pounds a week`)
                ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): income above the applicable amount would be a negative amount; section 124(1)(b) gives no entitlement then
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where a person is entitled to income support"

-- src:2674 | (5) Where a person is entitled to income support for a period to which this subsection applies, the amount payable for that period shall be calculated in such manner as may be prescribed.
@ref s 124(5) (src:2674)
GIVEN `s 124(6) subsection (5) applies to the period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount calculated in the manner prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 124(5) the amount payable for the period in pounds` MEANS
    IF `s 124(1) is known to hold` `s 124(6) subsection (5) applies to the period`
    THEN `the amount calculated in the manner prescribed`   -- NOTHING when the person does not have it: NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in such manner as may be prescribed"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a period to which this subsection applies"

-- (6): a period of less than a week, whether it is the whole period for which income support is payable (a)
-- or any other period (b).  A week is 7 days beginning with Sunday (s 122(1)), so a period of 1 to 6 days is
-- less than a week.
-- src:2675 | (6) Subsection (5) above applies—
-- src:2676 | (a) to a period of less than a week which is the whole period for which income support is payable; and
-- src:2677 | (b) to any other period of less than a week for which it is payable.
@ref s 124(6) (src:2675-2677)
GIVEN `the number of days in the period` IS A NUMBER
      `it is the whole period for which income support is payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 124(6) subsection (5) applies to the period` MEANS
    IF `the number of days in the period` AT LEAST 1 AND `the number of days in the period` LESS THAN 7
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- both paragraphs give the same answer: (a) the whole period, (b) any other period of less than a week
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a period of less than a week"

-- src:2678 | (7) In this section, “income-related employment and support allowance” means an income-related allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 (employment and support allowance).
@ref s 124(7) (src:2678)
GIVEN `the allowance is an income-related allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 (employment and support allowance)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 124(7) the allowance is an income-related employment and support allowance` MEANS
    IF `the allowance is an income-related allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 (employment and support allowance)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“income-related employment and support allowance” means"

§§ `s 126 -- trade disputes`

-- (2): the maternity period begins at the beginning of the 6th week before the expected week of confinement and
-- ends at the end of the 7th week after the week in which confinement takes place.  A week is 7 days beginning
-- with Sunday (s 122(1)); Day (a date) MODULO 7 is 0 for Sunday.  The 1st week before a week begins 7 days
-- earlier, the 6th 42 days earlier; the 7th week after ends 7 x 7 + 6 = 55 days after the confinement week begins.
-- src:2686 | (2) In subsection (1) above “the maternity period” means the period commencing at the beginning of the 6th week before the expected week of confinement and ending at the end of the 7th week after the week in which confinement takes place.
@ref s 126(2) (src:2686)
GIVEN `the expected date of confinement` IS A DATE
      `the date of confinement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A Period
`s 126(2) the maternity period` MEANS
    Period WITH
        `the first day` IS (`the first day of the Sunday week containing` `the expected date of confinement`) MINUS 42
        `the last day`  IS (`the first day of the Sunday week containing` `the date of confinement`) PLUS 55
    WHERE
        `the first day of the Sunday week containing` date MEANS date MINUS ((Day date) MODULO 7)

-- src:2682 | (1) This section applies to a person, other than a child or a person of a prescribed description—
-- src:2683 | (a) who is prevented from being entitled to a jobseeker’s allowance by section 14 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (trade disputes); or
-- src:2684 | (b) who would be so prevented if otherwise entitled to that benefit,
-- src:2685 | except during any period shown by the person to be a period of incapacity for work ... or to be within the maternity period.
@ref s 126(1) (src:2682-2685)
GIVEN `s 173(a) the person is under 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is of a prescribed description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is prevented from being entitled to a jobseeker's allowance by section 14 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (trade disputes)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would be so prevented if otherwise entitled to that benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period is one shown by the person to be a period of incapacity for work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period is one shown by the person to be within the maternity period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126(1) section 126 applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `s 124(1) is known to hold` `s 173(a) the person is under 16` OR `the person is of a prescribed description`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than a child or a person of a prescribed description" ("child" is a person under 16, s 137(1))
    ELSE
        IF NOT (    `the person is prevented from being entitled to a jobseeker's allowance by section 14 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (trade disputes)`
                OR `the person would be so prevented if otherwise entitled to that benefit`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person ... (a) who is prevented ... or (b) who would be so prevented"
        ELSE
            IF `the period is one shown by the person to be a period of incapacity for work` OR `the period is one shown by the person to be within the maternity period`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except during any period shown by the person to be a period of incapacity for work ... or to be within the maternity period"
            ELSE `s 124(1) holds or else nothing` (`s 124(1) does not hold` `s 173(a) the person is under 16`)

DECLARE `s 126(3) Case` IS ONE OF
    `s 126(3)(a) the person is not a member of a family`
    `s 126(3)(b) the person is a member of a family but not of a couple`
    `s 126(3)(c)(i) the section applies to one member of a couple and the applicable amount consists only of an amount in respect of them`
    `s 126(3)(c)(ii) the section applies to one member of a couple and the applicable amount includes other amounts`
    `s 126(3)(d)(i) the section applies to both members of a couple and neither is responsible for a child or a person of a prescribed description who is a member of the same household`
    `s 126(3)(d)(ii) the section applies to both members of a couple in any other case`

-- (4): where a reduction under (3)(c) would not produce a multiple of 5p, the reduction is to the nearest lower
-- multiple of 5p.
-- src:2696 | (4) Where a reduction under subsection (3)(c) above would not produce a sum which is a multiple of 5p, the reduction shall be to the nearest lower sum which is such a multiple.
@ref s 126(4) (src:2696)
GIVEN sum IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 126(4) the sum rounded down to a multiple of 5p` MEANS
    (FLOOR (sum DIVIDED BY 0.05)) TIMES 0.05

-- (3): the applicable amount to be used in calculating income support while the section applies.
-- (c)(i) halves the whole amount; (c)(ii) halves the portion in respect of the couple and drops the further
-- portion in respect of the member to whom the section applies.  Reading taken for (4) in (c)(ii): it is the
-- halved portion that is rounded down (fork F6 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2687 | (3) For the purpose of calculating income support—
-- src:2688 | (a) so long as this section applies to a person who is not a member of a family, the applicable amount shall be disregarded;
-- src:2689 | (b) so long as it applies to a person who is a member of a family but is not a member of a couple, the portion of the applicable amount which is included in respect of him shall be disregarded;
-- src:2690 | (c) so long as it applies to one of the members of a couple—
-- src:2691 | (i) if the applicable amount consists only of an amount in respect of them, it shall be reduced to one half; and
-- src:2692 | (ii) if it includes other amounts, the portion of it which is included in respect of them shall be reduced to one-half and any further portion of it which is included in respect of the member of the couple to whom this section applies shall be disregarded;
-- src:2693 | (d) so long as it applies to both the members of a couple—
-- src:2694 | (i) if neither of them is responsible for a child or person of a prescribed description who is a member of the same household, the applicable amount shall be disregarded; and
-- src:2695 | (ii) in any other case, the portion of the applicable amount which is included in respect of them and any further portion of it which is included in respect of either of them shall be disregarded.
@ref s 126(3) (src:2687-2695)
GIVEN case IS A `s 126(3) Case`
      `the applicable amount in pounds a week` IS A NUMBER
      `the portion of it included in respect of the person or of them` IS A NUMBER
      `any further portion of it included in respect of the member of the couple to whom the section applies, or of either of them` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 126(3) the applicable amount to be used in pounds a week` MEANS
    CONSIDER case
    WHEN `s 126(3)(a) the person is not a member of a family` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 126(3)(b) the person is a member of a family but not of a couple` THEN
        `the applicable amount in pounds a week` MINUS `the portion of it included in respect of the person or of them`
    WHEN `s 126(3)(c)(i) the section applies to one member of a couple and the applicable amount consists only of an amount in respect of them` THEN
        `s 126(4) the sum rounded down to a multiple of 5p` (`the applicable amount in pounds a week` DIVIDED BY 2)
    WHEN `s 126(3)(c)(ii) the section applies to one member of a couple and the applicable amount includes other amounts` THEN
        ((`the applicable amount in pounds a week` MINUS `the portion of it included in respect of the person or of them`)
         PLUS (`s 126(4) the sum rounded down to a multiple of 5p` (`the portion of it included in respect of the person or of them` DIVIDED BY 2)))
        MINUS `any further portion of it included in respect of the member of the couple to whom the section applies, or of either of them`
    WHEN `s 126(3)(d)(i) the section applies to both members of a couple and neither is responsible for a child or a person of a prescribed description who is a member of the same household` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 126(3)(d)(ii) the section applies to both members of a couple in any other case` THEN
        (`the applicable amount in pounds a week` MINUS `the portion of it included in respect of the person or of them`)
        MINUS `any further portion of it included in respect of the member of the couple to whom the section applies, or of either of them`

-- (5)(a): payments by reason of being without employment, and tax repayable under PAYE, are income and are not
-- disregarded, except so far as regulations provide otherwise.
-- src:2697 | (5) Where this section applies to a person for any period, then, except so far as regulations provide otherwise—
-- src:2698 | (a) in calculating the entitlement to income support of that person or a member of his family the following shall be treated as his income and shall not be disregarded—
-- src:2699 | (i) any payment which he or a member of his family receives or is entitled to obtain by reason of the person to whom this section applies being without employment for that period; and
-- src:2700 | (ii) without prejudice to the generality of sub-paragraph (i) above, any amount which becomes or would on an application duly made become available to him in that period by way of repayment of income tax deducted from his taxable earnings (as defined by section 10 of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003) under PAYE regulations; and
@ref s 126(5)(a) (src:2697-2700)
GIVEN `the income of the person or of a member of the person's family apart from the payments in (a)` IS A NUMBER
      `any payment received or obtainable by reason of being without employment for the period` IS A NUMBER
      `any amount which becomes or would on an application duly made become available by way of repayment of income tax deducted from taxable earnings under PAYE regulations` IS A NUMBER
      `regulations provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 126(5)(a) the income taken into account in pounds` MEANS
    IF `regulations provide otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "except so far as regulations provide otherwise"
    ELSE JUST (`the income of the person or of a member of the person's family apart from the payments in (a)`
               PLUS `any payment received or obtainable by reason of being without employment for the period`
               PLUS `any amount which becomes or would on an application duly made become available by way of repayment of income tax deducted from taxable earnings under PAYE regulations`)

-- (5)(b): income support for the period is not paid if its weekly rate is equal to or less than the relevant sum,
-- and otherwise is paid at the difference.
-- src:2701 | (b) any payment by way of income support for that period or any part of it which apart from this paragraph would be made to him, or to a person whose applicable amount is aggregated with his—
-- src:2702 | (i) shall not be made if the weekly rate of payment is equal to or less than the relevant sum; or
-- src:2703 | (ii) if it is more than the relevant sum, shall be at a weekly rate equal to the difference.
@ref s 126(5)(b) (src:2701-2703)
GIVEN `the weekly rate that would apart from paragraph (b) be paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the relevant sum in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `regulations provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 126(5)(b) the weekly rate of income support payable in pounds` MEANS
    IF `regulations provide otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "except so far as regulations provide otherwise"
    ELSE
        IF `the weekly rate that would apart from paragraph (b) be paid` AT MOST `the relevant sum in pounds`
        THEN JUST 0   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be made if the weekly rate of payment is equal to or less than the relevant sum"
        ELSE JUST (`the weekly rate that would apart from paragraph (b) be paid` MINUS `the relevant sum in pounds`)

-- (7): the relevant sum is £53.00, subject to (8): after an order under s 150 of the Administration Act the sum
-- is the substituted sum the order states.
-- src:2705 | (7) Subject to subsection (8) below, “the relevant sum” for the purposes of subsection (5) above shall be £53.00.
@ref s 126(7) (src:2705)
GIVEN `the substituted sum the latest order states, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 126(7) the relevant sum in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the substituted sum the latest order states, if there is one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 53.00
    WHEN JUST substituted THEN substituted

-- (8): the substituted sum is the sum increased by the percentage by which the single person's personal
-- allowance (aged not less than 25) was increased; if not a multiple of 50p, a remainder of 25p is disregarded
-- (rounds down) and any other remainder rounds to the nearest 50p.  The remainder is the excess over the last
-- multiple of 50p at or below the increased sum (fork F7 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2706 | (8) If an order under section 150 of the Administration Act (annual up-rating) has the effect of increasing payments of income support, from the time when the order comes into force there shall be substituted, in subsection (5)(b) above, for the references to the sum for the time being mentioned in it references to a sum arrived at by—
-- src:2707 | (a) increasing that sum by the percentage by which the personal allowance under paragraph 1(1) of Part I of Schedule 2 to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 for a single person aged not less than 25 has been increased by the order; and
-- src:2708 | (b) if the sum as so increased is not a multiple of 50p, disregarding the remainder if it is 25p and, if it is not, rounding it up or down to the nearest 50p,
-- src:2709 | and the order shall state the substituted sum.
@ref s 126(8) (src:2706-2709)
GIVEN `the sum for the time being mentioned in subsection (5)(b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage by which the personal allowance has been increased` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 126(8) the substituted sum in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the remainder` EQUALS 0
    THEN `the increased sum`
    ELSE
        IF `the remainder` EQUALS 0.25
        THEN `the increased sum` MINUS `the remainder`
        ELSE 0.5 TIMES (ROUND (`the increased sum` DIVIDED BY 0.5))
    WHERE
        `the increased sum` MEANS `the sum for the time being mentioned in subsection (5)(b)` TIMES (1 PLUS (`the percentage by which the personal allowance has been increased` DIVIDED BY 100))
        `the remainder` MEANS `the increased sum` MINUS (0.5 TIMES (FLOOR (`the increased sum` DIVIDED BY 0.5)))

§§ `s 127 -- effect of return to work`

-- (a): s 126 ceases to apply at the commencement of the day on which the person returns to work with the same
-- employer after a period during which it applied.
-- src:2711 | If a person returns to work with the same employer after a period during which section 126 above applies to him, and whether or not his return is before the end of any stoppage of work in relation to which he is or would be prevented from being entitled to a jobseeker’s allowance—
-- src:2712 | (a) that section shall cease to apply to him at the commencement of the day on which he returns to work; and
@ref s 127(a) (src:2711-2712)
GIVEN `the person returned to work with the same employer after a period during which section 126 applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person returned to work` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(a) section 126 applies to the person on the day` MEANS
    IF `the person returned to work with the same employer after a period during which section 126 applied` AND `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the day the person returned to work`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that section shall cease to apply to him at the commencement of the day on which he returns to work"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): before the return, section 127 says nothing about whether section 126 applies

-- (b): until the end of the period of 15 days beginning with that day, s 124(1) has effect with a substituted
-- paragraph (c).  The 15 days are the day of return and the 14 days after it.
-- src:2711 | If a person returns to work with the same employer after a period during which section 126 above applies to him, and whether or not his return is before the end of any stoppage of work in relation to which he is or would be prevented from being entitled to a jobseeker’s allowance—
-- src:2712 | (a) that section shall cease to apply to him at the commencement of the day on which he returns to work; and
-- src:2713 | (b) until the end of the period of 15 days beginning with that day, section 124(1) above shall have effect in relation to him as if the following paragraph were substituted for paragraph (c)—
-- src:2714 | (c) in the case of a member of a couple, the other member is not engaged in remunerative work; and
@ref s 127(b) (src:2711-2714)
GIVEN `the person returned to work with the same employer after a period during which section 126 applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person returned to work` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(b) section 124(1) has effect with the substituted paragraph (c) on the day` MEANS
    IF     `the person returned to work with the same employer after a period during which section 126 applied`
       AND `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the day the person returned to work`
       AND `the day asked about` AT MOST (`the day the person returned to work` PLUS 14)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "until the end of the period of 15 days beginning with that day"

DECLARE `s 127(c) Party` IS ONE OF
    `s 127(c) the person to whom the sum was paid`
    `s 127(c) a prescribed person`
    `s 127(c) the other member of the couple`

-- (c): a sum paid by way of income support for the 15 days is recoverable in accordance with the regulations from
-- the person paid, any prescribed person, or (where the person paid is a member of a couple) the other member.
-- src:2715 | (c) any sum paid by way of income support for that period of 15 days to him or, where he is a member of a couple, to the other member of that couple, shall be recoverable in accordance with the regulations from the person to whom it was paid or from any prescribed person or, where the person to whom it was paid is a member of a couple, from the other member of the couple.
@ref s 127(c) (src:2715)
GIVEN `the sum was paid by way of income support for that period of 15 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      party IS A `s 127(c) Party`
      `the person to whom it was paid is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(c) the sum is recoverable in accordance with the regulations from the party` MEANS
    IF `the sum was paid by way of income support for that period of 15 days`
    THEN
        CONSIDER party
        WHEN `s 127(c) the person to whom the sum was paid` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 127(c) a prescribed person` THEN
            IF `the person is a prescribed person` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "any prescribed person"
        WHEN `s 127(c) the other member of the couple` THEN
            IF `the person to whom it was paid is a member of a couple` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the person to whom it was paid is a member of a couple"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any sum paid by way of income support for that period of 15 days"

§§ `s 130 -- housing benefit`

-- 130A(1): the appropriate maximum housing benefit (the AMHB) is determined under this section, that is
-- as the regulations prescribe (130A(2)); the amount is therefore an input.
-- src:2739 | (1) For the purposes of section 130 above, the appropriate maximum housing benefit (in this section referred to as “the AMHB”) is determined in accordance with this section.
-- src:2740 | (2) Regulations must prescribe the manner in which the AMHB is to be determined.
@ref s 130A(1) (src:2739-2740)
GIVEN `the amount determined in the manner the regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 130A(1) the appropriate maximum housing benefit in pounds` MEANS
    `the amount determined in the manner the regulations prescribe`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when the person has no such amount: "Regulations must prescribe the manner in which the AMHB is to be determined"

-- src:2747 | (7) A rent officer determination is a determination made by a rent officer in the exercise of functions under section 122 of the Housing Act 1996.
@ref s 130A(7) (src:2747)
GIVEN `the determination is one made by a rent officer in the exercise of functions under section 122 of the Housing Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130A(7) the determination is a rent officer determination` MEANS
    IF `the determination is one made by a rent officer in the exercise of functions under section 122 of the Housing Act 1996`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "A rent officer determination is a determination made by..." says what one is, not what else is not

-- (2): "payments in respect of a dwelling" means such payments as may be prescribed, but the power does not
-- include council tax payments or mortgage payments.
-- src:2730 | (2) In subsection (1) above “payments in respect of a dwelling” means such payments as may be prescribed, but the power to prescribe payments does not include power to prescribe—
-- src:2731 | (a) payments to a billing authority or to a local authority in Scotland in respect of council tax;
-- src:2732 | (b) mortgage payments, or, in relation to Scotland, payments under heritable securities.
@ref s 130(2) (src:2730-2732)
GIVEN `the payment is one prescribed as a payment in respect of a dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is one to a billing authority or to a local authority in Scotland in respect of council tax` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is a mortgage payment or, in Scotland, a payment under a heritable security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(2) the payment is a payment in respect of a dwelling` MEANS
    IF `the payment is one to a billing authority or to a local authority in Scotland in respect of council tax` OR `the payment is a mortgage payment or, in Scotland, a payment under a heritable security`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the power to prescribe payments does not include power to prescribe— (a) payments to a billing authority ... in respect of council tax; (b) mortgage payments"
    ELSE
        IF `the payment is one prescribed as a payment in respect of a dwelling`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“payments in respect of a dwelling” means such payments as may be prescribed"

-- (1): a person is entitled to housing benefit if liable for payments on a dwelling in Great Britain that is the
-- person's home, there is an AMHB, and either income does not exceed the applicable amount or the excess is
-- so small that, after the (3)(b) deduction, something remains.
-- src:2724 | (1) A person is entitled to housing benefit if—
-- src:2725 | (a) he is liable to make payments in respect of a dwelling in Great Britain which he occupies as his home;
-- src:2726 | (b) there is an appropriate maximum housing benefit in his case; and
-- src:2727 | (c) either—
-- src:2728 | (i) he has no income or his income does not exceed the applicable amount; or
-- src:2729 | (ii) his income exceeds that amount, but only by so much that there is an amount remaining if the deduction for which subsection (3)(b) below provides is made.
@ref s 130(1) (src:2724-2729)
GIVEN `the person is liable to make payments in respect of a dwelling in Great Britain which the person occupies as the person's home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 130A(1) the appropriate maximum housing benefit in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the person has no income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's income in pounds a week` IS A NUMBER
      `the applicable amount in pounds a week` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed rate of deduction from the excess of income over the applicable amount, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(1) the person is entitled to housing benefit` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is entitled to housing benefit if" -- a failed condition gives JUST FALSE
    `s 124(1) all of these hold` (LIST
        JUST `the person is liable to make payments in respect of a dwelling in Great Britain which the person occupies as the person's home`
        , `paragraph (b)`
        , `paragraph (c)`)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 130A(1) the appropriate maximum housing benefit in pounds`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST amount THEN JUST TRUE
        `the excess` MEANS `the person's income in pounds a week` MINUS `the applicable amount in pounds a week`
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS
            IF `the person has no income` OR `the person's income in pounds a week` AT MOST `the applicable amount in pounds a week`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                CONSIDER `s 130A(1) the appropriate maximum housing benefit in pounds`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST amount THEN JUST (amount MINUS (`the prescribed rate of deduction from the excess of income over the applicable amount, as a fraction` TIMES `the excess`) GREATER THAN 0)

-- (3): the amount is the AMHB, less prescribed percentages of the excess of income over the applicable amount.
-- src:2733 | (3) Where a person is entitled to housing benefit, then—
-- src:2734 | (a) if he has no income or his income does not exceed the applicable amount, the amount of the housing benefit shall be the amount which is the appropriate maximum housing benefit in his case; and
-- src:2735 | (b) if his income exceeds the applicable amount, the amount of the housing benefit shall be what remains after the deduction from the appropriate maximum housing benefit of prescribed percentages of the excess of his income over the applicable amount.
@ref s 130(3) (src:2733-2735)
GIVEN `s 130(1) the person is entitled to housing benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 130A(1) the appropriate maximum housing benefit in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the person has no income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's income in pounds a week` IS A NUMBER
      `the applicable amount in pounds a week` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed rate of deduction from the excess of income over the applicable amount, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 130(3) the amount of housing benefit in pounds a week` MEANS
    IF `s 124(1) is known to hold` `s 130(1) the person is entitled to housing benefit`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `s 130A(1) the appropriate maximum housing benefit in pounds`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the AMHB is prescribed by regulations (section 130A(2))
        WHEN JUST amount THEN
            IF `the person has no income` OR `the person's income in pounds a week` AT MOST `the applicable amount in pounds a week`
            THEN JUST amount
            ELSE JUST (amount MINUS (`the prescribed rate of deduction from the excess of income over the applicable amount, as a fraction` TIMES (`the person's income in pounds a week` MINUS `the applicable amount in pounds a week`)))
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person is entitled to housing benefit"

§§ `ss 134 to 136A -- exclusions, applicable amount, income and capital`

-- 134(1): "No person shall be entitled to an income-related benefit if his capital or a prescribed part of it
-- exceeds the prescribed amount."  The function is named for the bar's own condition ("by capital"), so it tests
-- that condition: JUST TRUE when the bar applies and JUST FALSE when it does not.  It says nothing of entitlement
-- (the subsection bars; it does not grant).
-- src:2769 | (1) No person shall be entitled to an income-related benefit if his capital or a prescribed part of it exceeds the prescribed amount.
@ref s 134(1) (src:2769)
GIVEN `the person's capital in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed part of the capital in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(1) the person is barred from the income-related benefit by capital` MEANS
    IF `the person's capital in pounds` GREATER THAN `the prescribed amount in pounds` OR `the prescribed part of the capital in pounds` GREATER THAN `the prescribed amount in pounds`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the text says no in its own words: "No person shall be entitled to an income-related benefit if his capital or a prescribed part of it exceeds the prescribed amount"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be entitled to an income-related benefit if his capital or a prescribed part of it exceeds the prescribed amount" -- the "if" is not met, so the bar by capital does not apply (reading (a))

-- src:2770 | (2) Except in prescribed circumstances the entitlement of one member of a family to any one income-related benefit excludes entitlement to that benefit for any other member for the same period.
@ref s 134(2) (src:2770)
GIVEN `another member of the person's family is entitled to the same income-related benefit for the same period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances are prescribed ones` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(2) the person's entitlement is excluded by another member's entitlement` MEANS
    IF `another member of the person's family is entitled to the same income-related benefit for the same period` AND (NOT `the circumstances are prescribed ones`)
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the text says no in its own words: "the entitlement of one member of a family to any one income-related benefit excludes entitlement to that benefit for any other member for the same period"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except in prescribed circumstances the entitlement of one member of a family to any one income-related benefit excludes entitlement to that benefit for any other member for the same period" -- no other member is entitled, or the circumstances are prescribed ones, so the exclusion does not apply

-- src:2772 | (4) Where the amount of any income-related benefit would be less than a prescribed amount, it shall not be payable except in prescribed circumstances.
@ref s 134(4) (src:2772)
GIVEN `the amount of the benefit in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the circumstances are prescribed ones` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(4) the income-related benefit is not payable` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the benefit in pounds` LESS THAN `the prescribed amount in pounds` AND (NOT `the circumstances are prescribed ones`)
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the text says no in its own words: "it shall not be payable except in prescribed circumstances"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the amount ... would be less than a prescribed amount"

-- src:2774 | (1) The applicable amount, in relation to any income-related benefit, shall be such amount or the aggregate of such amounts as may be prescribed in relation to that benefit.
-- src:2775 | (2) The power to prescribe applicable amounts conferred by subsection (1) above includes power to prescribe nil as an applicable amount.
@ref s 135(1) (src:2774-2775)
GIVEN `the amounts prescribed in relation to the benefit` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 135(1) the applicable amount in pounds` MEANS
    sum `the amounts prescribed in relation to the benefit`   -- "such amount or the aggregate of such amounts"; subsection (2): nil (an empty list, or amounts of 0) is allowed

-- src:2778 | (5) ... the applicable amount for a severely disabled person shall include an amount in respect of his being a severely disabled person.
@ref s 135(5) (src:2778)
GIVEN `the person is a severely disabled person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135(5) the applicable amount includes an amount for being severely disabled` MEANS
    IF `the person is a severely disabled person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the applicable amount for a severely disabled person shall include"

-- 136(1): the income and capital of any member of the family is treated as the claimant's, except in prescribed
-- circumstances.  One function serves both: pass the members' incomes, or the members' capital.
-- src:2781 | (1) Where a person claiming an income-related benefit is a member of a family, the income and capital of any member of that family shall, except in prescribed circumstances, be treated as the income and capital of that person.
@ref s 136(1) (src:2781)
GIVEN `the person claiming is a member of a family` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amounts of each member of the family, the claimant's own included` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the circumstances are prescribed ones` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 136(1) the amount treated as the claimant's in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the person claiming is a member of a family` AND (NOT `the circumstances are prescribed ones`)
    THEN JUST (sum `the amounts of each member of the family, the claimant's own included`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person claiming an income-related benefit is a member of a family ... except in prescribed circumstances"

DECLARE `s 136A(1) Benefit asked about` IS ONE OF
    `s 136A(1) housing benefit`
    `s 136A(1) council tax benefit`
    `s 136A(1) another income-related benefit`

-- src:2791 | (1) Subsections (2) and (3) below apply in relation to housing benefit and council tax benefit in the case of any person who has attained the qualifying age for state pension credit.
@ref s 136A(1) (src:2791)
GIVEN benefit IS A `s 136A(1) Benefit asked about`
      `the person has attained the qualifying age for state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136A(1) subsections (2) and (3) apply to the benefit and the person` MEANS
    IF `the person has attained the qualifying age for state pension credit`
    THEN
        CONSIDER benefit
        WHEN `s 136A(1) housing benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 136A(1) council tax benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 136A(1) another income-related benefit` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to housing benefit and council tax benefit"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of any person who has attained the qualifying age for state pension credit"

§§ `s 137(1) -- the definitions for Part VII`

-- A gloss: a "couple" is two people who are married or civil partners and share a household, or who are
-- not married or civil partners but live together as if they were.  The "prescribed circumstances" in
-- limb two are regulations' to supply, so the person states whether they apply.  The two limbs are a closed
-- "means": spouses who are not members of the same household fall under neither (fork F8 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2808 | “couple” means—
-- src:2809 | two people who are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are members of the same household; or
-- src:2810 | two people who are not married to, or civil partners of, each other but are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners otherwise than in prescribed circumstances;
@ref s 137(1) “couple” (src:2808-2810)
GIVEN couple IS A Couple
      `the circumstances are ones prescribed to take the pair out of limb two` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(1) the two persons are a couple` MEANS
    IF `limb one` OR `limb two`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“couple” means—"
    WHERE
        `limb one` MEANS
            (couple's `married to each other` OR couple's `civil partners of each other`)
            AND couple's `members of the same household`
        `limb two` MEANS
                (NOT (couple's `married to each other` OR couple's `civil partners of each other`))
            AND couple's `living together as if married or civil partners`
            AND (NOT `the circumstances are ones prescribed to take the pair out of limb two`)

-- The qualifying age for state pension credit: a woman's pensionable age; a man's is the age that is
-- pensionable age for a woman born on the same day as he was.  "Pensionable age" is borrowed (Pensions Act
-- 1995), so the date a woman born on the man's birthday attains it is a fact the person states.
-- src:2827 | “the qualifying age for state pension credit” is (in accordance with section 1(2)(b) and (6) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002)—
-- src:2828 | in the case of a woman, pensionable age; or
-- src:2829 | in the case of a man, the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day as the man;
@ref s 137(1) “the qualifying age for state pension credit” (src:2827-2829)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      `the date a woman born on the same day as the man would attain pensionable age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 137(1) the date the person attains the qualifying age for state pension credit` MEANS
    CONSIDER person's `sex`
    WHEN Woman THEN person's `date of attaining pensionable age`
    WHEN Man THEN `the date a woman born on the same day as the man would attain pensionable age`

-- src:2827 | “the qualifying age for state pension credit” is (in accordance with section 1(2)(b) and (6) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002)—
-- src:2828 | in the case of a woman, pensionable age; or
-- src:2829 | in the case of a man, the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day as the man;
@ref s 137(1) “the qualifying age for state pension credit” (src:2827-2829)
GIVEN `the date the person attains the qualifying age` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 137(1) the person has attained the qualifying age for state pension credit` MEANS
    `the date asked about` AT LEAST `the date the person attains the qualifying age`

-- src:2807 | “child” means a person under the age of 16;
@ref s 137(1) “child” (src:2807)
GIVEN `s 173(a) the person is under 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(1) the person is a child` MEANS
    `s 173(a) the person is under 16`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words), via s 173(a)'s JUST FALSE: "“child” means a person under the age of 16"

-- src:2813 | “dwelling” means any residential accommodation, whether or not consisting of the whole or part of a building and whether or not comprising separate and self-contained premises;
@ref s 137(1) “dwelling” (src:2813)
GIVEN `the accommodation is residential accommodation, whether or not it is the whole or part of a building and whether or not it is separate and self-contained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(1) the accommodation is a dwelling` MEANS
    IF `the accommodation is residential accommodation, whether or not it is the whole or part of a building and whether or not it is separate and self-contained`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“dwelling” means any residential accommodation"

-- "family" means (a) a couple; (b) a couple and a member of the same household for whom one or both is
-- responsible who is a child or a person of a prescribed description; (c) except in prescribed circumstances,
-- a person who is not a member of a couple and a member of the same household for whom that person is
-- responsible and who is a child or a person of a prescribed description.
-- src:2814 | “family” means—
-- src:2815 | a couple;
-- src:2816 | a couple and a member of the same household for whom one of them is or both are responsible and who is a child or a person of a prescribed description;
-- src:2817 | except in prescribed circumstances, a person who is not a member of a couple and a member of the same household for whom that person is responsible and who is a child or a person of a prescribed description;
@ref s 137(1) “family” (src:2814-2817)
GIVEN `the persons are a couple` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a member of the same household for whom one or both of the couple is or are responsible is a child or a person of a prescribed description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member of the same household for whom the person is responsible is a child or a person of a prescribed description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances are prescribed ones in which limb (c) does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(1) the persons are a family` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“family” means—" -- when no limb holds, JUST FALSE
    `s 124(1) either holds` (`s 124(1) either holds` `limb (a)` `limb (b)`) `limb (c)`
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS `the persons are a couple`
        `limb (b)` MEANS
            `s 124(1) both hold` `the persons are a couple`
                (JUST `a member of the same household for whom one or both of the couple is or are responsible is a child or a person of a prescribed description`)
        `limb (c)` MEANS
            JUST (    `the person is not a member of a couple`
                  AND `a member of the same household for whom the person is responsible is a child or a person of a prescribed description`
                  AND (NOT `the circumstances are prescribed ones in which limb (c) does not apply`))

-- "In this Part of this Act, unless the context otherwise requires": a defined meaning applies unless the context
-- otherwise requires.  Whether it does is a judgment, taken as a plain input.
-- src:2805 | (1) In this Part of this Act, unless the context otherwise requires—
@ref s 137(1) (src:2805)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(1) the defined meaning applies` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part of this Act, unless the context otherwise requires" -- the context otherwise requires, so the defined meaning does not apply
    ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 137(1) Kind of scheme` IS ONE OF
    `s 137(1) a scheme made under Schedule 8 to this Act`
    `s 137(1) a scheme made under section 159 of the 1975 Act`
    `s 137(1) a scheme made under the Old Cases Act`
    `s 137(1) a scheme of another kind`

-- src:2819 | “industrial injuries scheme” means a scheme made under Schedule 8 to this Act or section 159 of the 1975 Act or under the Old Cases Act;
@ref s 137(1) “industrial injuries scheme” (src:2819)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 137(1) Kind of scheme`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(1) the scheme is an industrial injuries scheme` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 137(1) a scheme of another kind` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“industrial injuries scheme” means a scheme made under Schedule 8 to this Act or section 159 of the 1975 Act or under the Old Cases Act"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2821 | “local authority” in relation to Scotland means a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994;
@ref s 137(1) “local authority” (src:2821)
GIVEN `the body is a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(1) the body is a local authority in relation to Scotland` MEANS
    IF `the body is a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“local authority” in relation to Scotland means a council constituted under section 2"

-- src:2832 | “war pension scheme” means a scheme under which war pensions (as defined in section 25 of the Social Security Act 1989) are provided;
@ref s 137(1) “war pension scheme” (src:2832)
GIVEN `the scheme is one under which war pensions (as defined in section 25 of the Social Security Act 1989) are provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137(1) the scheme is a war pension scheme` MEANS
    IF `the scheme is one under which war pensions (as defined in section 25 of the Social Security Act 1989) are provided`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“war pension scheme” means a scheme under which war pensions ... are provided"

-- "week", in relation to council tax benefit, is 7 days beginning with a Monday.  Day (a date) MODULO 7 is 0 for
-- Sunday and 1 for Monday, so a date is (Day date + 6) MODULO 7 days after the Monday that begins its week.
-- src:2833 | “week”, in relation to council tax benefit, means a period of 7 days beginning with a Monday.
@ref s 137(1) “week” (src:2833)
GIVEN date IS A DATE
GIVETH A Period
`s 137(1) the week in relation to council tax benefit containing the date` MEANS
    Period WITH
        `the first day` IS date MINUS (((Day date) PLUS 6) MODULO 7)
        `the last day`  IS (date MINUS (((Day date) PLUS 6) MODULO 7)) PLUS 6

DECLARE `s 137(1) Defined term` IS ONE OF
    `s 137(1) billing authority`
    `s 137(1) income-based jobseeker's allowance`
    `s 137(1) pensionable age`
    `s 137(1) prescribed`
    `s 137(1) state pension credit`

-- The terms of s 137(1) that are tests on facts have functions above.  These are the ones the Act fixes by
-- pointing at another Act, or by a plain statement.
-- src:2806 | “billing authority” has the same meaning as in Part I of the Local Government Finance Act 1992;
-- src:2807 | “child” means a person under the age of 16;
-- src:2808 | “couple” means—
-- src:2809 | two people who are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are members of the same household; or
-- src:2810 | two people who are not married to, or civil partners of, each other but are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners otherwise than in prescribed circumstances;
-- src:2813 | “dwelling” means any residential accommodation, whether or not consisting of the whole or part of a building and whether or not comprising separate and self-contained premises;
-- src:2814 | “family” means—
-- src:2815 | a couple;
-- src:2816 | a couple and a member of the same household for whom one of them is or both are responsible and who is a child or a person of a prescribed description;
-- src:2817 | except in prescribed circumstances, a person who is not a member of a couple and a member of the same household for whom that person is responsible and who is a child or a person of a prescribed description;
-- src:2818 | “income-based jobseeker’s allowance” has the same meaning as in the Jobseekers Act 1995;
-- src:2819 | “industrial injuries scheme” means a scheme made under Schedule 8 to this Act or section 159 of the 1975 Act or under the Old Cases Act;
-- src:2821 | “local authority” in relation to Scotland means a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994;
-- src:2825 | “pensionable age” has the meaning given by the rules in paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Pensions Act 1995 (c. 26);
-- src:2826 | “prescribed”means specified in or determined in accordance with regulations;
-- src:2827 | “the qualifying age for state pension credit” is (in accordance with section 1(2)(b) and (6) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002)—
-- src:2828 | in the case of a woman, pensionable age; or
-- src:2829 | in the case of a man, the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day as the man;
-- src:2830 | “state pension credit” means state pension credit under the State Pension Credit Act 2002;
@ref s 137(1) (src:2806-2830)
GIVEN term IS A `s 137(1) Defined term`
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 137(1) how the term is defined` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `s 137(1) billing authority` THEN
        `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
            `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
            `what it points at or says` IS "the same meaning as in Part I of the Local Government Finance Act 1992"
    WHEN `s 137(1) income-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN
        `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
            `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
            `what it points at or says` IS "the same meaning as in the Jobseekers Act 1995"
    WHEN `s 137(1) pensionable age` THEN
        `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
            `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
            `what it points at or says` IS "the meaning given by the rules in paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Pensions Act 1995 (c. 26)"
    WHEN `s 137(1) prescribed` THEN
        `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
            `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
            `what it points at or says` IS "specified in or determined in accordance with regulations"
    WHEN `s 137(1) state pension credit` THEN
        `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
            `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
            `what it points at or says` IS "state pension credit under the State Pension Credit Act 2002"

DECLARE `s 136A(5) Defined term` IS ONE OF
    `s 136A(5) assessed amount`
    `s 136A(5) element`
    `s 136A(5) retirement provision`

-- src:2801 | (5) In subsection (4) above “assessed amount”, “element” and “retirement provision” have the same meaning as in the State Pension Credit Act 2002.
@ref s 136A(5) (src:2801)
GIVEN term IS A `s 136A(5) Defined term`
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 136A(5) how the term is defined` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a meaning borrowed from another Act or instrument`
        `what it points at or says` IS "the same meaning as in the State Pension Credit Act 2002"
